{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 27, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 27, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=28&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=26&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 667127718, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r667127718-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Just awesome", "text": "We were thrilled to enter this temple and be enveloped in a different scene from the rest of the city altogether. A must see temple for all who visit Nepal. We were awestruck by the beauty of the architecture and the holiness of the entire place. Very wonderful experience. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "987E9AC705618DA6B20A7CE1CF658DA2", "name": "radharani9", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/radharani9", "username": "radharani9", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f4/5d/default-avatar-2020-32.jpg", "contribution_count": 196, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1155906, "location_name": "Puttaparthi", "location_name_detailed": "Puttaparthi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-04-17", "published_at_date": "2019-04-17"}, {"review_id": 667098130, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r667098130-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A bit discouraging and disorientating", "text": "The lack of signage and direction is what makes this place so frustrating. We wandered around not really knowing where to go until we were barked at by staff and redirected to a poorly advertised ticket booth. After paying 1000 Nepalese Rupee each we were asked if we wanted a guide and we declined. We appreciated the offer but had already paid for a few guides at previous attractions and just wanted to go at our own pace this time. We had sort of assumed that if we made our way up to the river we would be able to see the cremations taking place but we seemed to be fenced off from the river so we followed along the fence line trying to find out how we could see the river. Other people seemed to be standing on the other side of the fence but we could never work out how they got there which was so frustrating. And it wasn’t just a matter of staring through the bars because there was two lots of fencing with a gap in the middle so we couldn’t get close enough. None of the other tourists seemed to have a guide and even though the temple grounds cover a vast area we seemed to quickly exhaust the areas that were accessible. \n\nThere were these huge concrete steps that seemed to go on forever but we were pretty reluctant to go to the top of those. We didn’t really know where they led and we were struggling a bit with the air quality so getting up those steps really did feel like going up Mt Everest. We realised though that everywhere else was a bit of a dead end and having paid for the attraction we wanted to get some value out of the experience. Once we got to the top we followed along a path that seemed to go on forever. People were walking in the opposite direction so we were concerned that at the end of this trek we may have to turn around and the stairs had started to descend so it wouldn’t all be downhill on the return. I felt as though we were walking parallel with the river but the river was completely obscured from view, we could only see snatches of it through gaps in the trees. Perhaps there were no cremations happening that day or perhaps I didn’t really understand the point of the tourist attraction. We speculated that they intentionally make it so unclear so people resort to paying for a guide but we were too stubborn. Anyway, after walking for what seemed like forever we exited the temple on the opposite side which did lead us out to the river but there was nothing particular to see there. \n\nI don’t mean to sound so whingey but it did cost us 2000 Rupee altogether. Overall it was a bit disappointing.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5E8DB6B31311953BD33D7F0949F69B53", "name": "Aussie_Binturong", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Aussie_Binturong", "username": "Aussie_Binturong", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/5a/default-avatar-2020-36.jpg", "contribution_count": 405, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255067, "location_name": "Queensland", "location_name_detailed": "Queensland, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-04-17", "published_at_date": "2019-04-17"}, {"review_id": 667076443, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r667076443-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Need to repair", "text": "can visit this temple but as hindu .but hard to find even a toilet. the infrastructure is too old and need to repair most of the things ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "46F58656B8153FC67E806C04F955AFC3", "name": "Ichiban321", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Ichiban321", "username": "Ichiban321", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/df/99/default-avatar-2020-40.jpg", "contribution_count": 5, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-04-17", "published_at_date": "2019-04-17"}, {"review_id": 666971763, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r666971763-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Major Hindu Temple", "text": "This is the main Hindu temple in Kathmandu.  Unfortunately it is only open to Hindu.  Non-believers can circle outside and peek over the walls to see some of the icons and activities.  Some activities also spill outside.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2C58B08FFD194F00A55D3073E973E54B", "name": "Hockeydad900", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Hockeydad900", "username": "Hockeydad900", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 491, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 32573, "location_name": "La Canada Flintridge", "location_name_detailed": "La Canada Flintridge, California"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-04-16", "published_at_date": "2019-04-16"}, {"review_id": 666876150, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r666876150-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not for the faint hearted. ", "text": "Major cremation site for Kathmandu Hindus. All through the day and night bodies are cremated on platforms on the river bank. Although slightly macabre it is a fascinating spectacle. Further along from the Ghatts are structures containing Shiva Lingams and here you will find Saddhus ( holy men). There is also one of Hindus most sacred temples containing a huge statue of Nandi (Shivas Bull) although sadly only Hindus can enter. But you can stand at the gate and catch a view of his back end. An interesting place to spend a couple of hours . ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "43D87F4A0341775889BFABB29A835AC9", "name": "karmabuddha", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/karmabuddha", "username": "karmabuddha", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ee/10/default-avatar-2020-8.jpg", "contribution_count": 110, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 503974, "location_name": "Cleethorpes", "location_name_detailed": "Cleethorpes, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-04-16", "published_at_date": "2019-04-16"}, {"review_id": 666821273, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r666821273-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Very nice temple", "text": "Visited the temple and had dharshan of Lord pashupatinath ji .the temple is beautiful and all the small temples around main temple are very beautiful. God bless you all.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "70A99995B36E79C5CB4A86DBADF9204C", "name": "P L Thakur", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/thakur87", "username": "thakur87", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/26/0a/66/9e/thakur87.jpg", "contribution_count": 467, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554, "location_name": "Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/17/2e/56/7b/img-20190415-125949-largejpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-04-16", "published_at_date": "2019-04-16"}, {"review_id": 666685401, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r666685401-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Intriguing and possibly disturbing experience", "text": "Pashupati Nath Temple is supposedly one of the holiest places for Hindus. Temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva and only Hindus are permitted to enter. Right next to it is the Temple of Guheshwori on the banks of the holy Bagmati river. There you can witness cremations on raised platforms going on nonstop. A very unique experience for an outsider to say the least.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "EE5CDD74D3A923D6A61F489BEA548ACD", "name": "TLS71", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/TLS71", "username": "TLS71", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/9f/94/cf/tls71.jpg", "contribution_count": 36, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 274707, "location_name": "Prague", "location_name_detailed": "Prague, Czech Republic"}, "is_verified": false}, "im